{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792764163,"nonce":"CswQ285jUe2LObXCcKpQtJ5Jrrg=","title":"Interpreter-first startup fails benchmark kernels and replays main on bailout","message":"Verified at 75069892e50b64a7f962a99ac6c9d002aefc138a with the rebuilt release CLI. A fast-start policy cannot safely replace the existing eager native default yet.\n\nUnmodified benchmark sources, each with a fresh project cache:\n  target/release/rayzor run --release --tier-start-interpreted true --cache-dir /tmp/\u003cunique-cache\u003e compiler/benchmarks/src/\u003ckernel\u003e.hx\n\nFailures:\n- deltablue: SIGSEGV, fault 0x10 outside registered JIT code.\n- fannkuchredux: W0020, fannkuch return type Ptr(Void) with a valueless Return, then a trap-stub SIGABRT. Also fails with native start and RAYZOR_OPT_LEVEL=0 or 1 in the startup sweep, so the faster MIR pipelines expose a lowering/codegen defect rather than an interpreter-only problem.\n- revcomp and regexredux: Interpreter error: Cannot convert String(\"\u003eONE Homo sapiens alu\\n\") to i64.\n\nThe remaining eight instrumented benchmark processes completed but entered main twice after hot-loop bailout. A standalone minimal source confirms observable replay:\n  class Main { static function main() { trace(\"SIDE_EFFECT\"); var i = 0; while (i \u003c 2000) i++; trace(i); } }\nThe interpreter-first invocation prints SIDE_EFFECT twice followed by 2000. The default native invocation must print it once. execute_function handles JitBailout by compiling all modules and recursively re-executing the original function with its original arguments, not by resuming its frame. Startup hooks are also rerun by the baseline compilation path and must be audited for duplicated side effects.\n\nAcceptance: all 12 CI kernels should have matching observable results in interpreter-first and native startup; promotion must resume the suspended computation without replaying user-visible effects; O0/O1 must produce valid code without depending on O2 to mask invalid MIR. Do not flip the CLI start_interpreted policy until these conditions hold.\n\nEvidence: /tmp/rayzor-startup-audit/original-failures.json; *-original-interpreted.stderr; replay.hx and replay.stdout; optimization-sweep/results.json; the three-round sweep in results.json. No repository source changes were made for this investigation.","files":null}]}